Kurokesu libcamera packaging notes
==================================

This package is a Kurokesu fork of Raspberry Pi's libcamera packaging.
The recipe lives on a single DEP-14 `debian/latest` branch and reuses
RPi's recipe verbatim where possible. Deviations are kept minimal,
profile-driven, and tracked here so they can be retired when no longer
needed.

Supported suites
----------------

  * trixie: build with `--profiles=nodoc`.
  * bookworm: build with
    `--profiles=pkg.libcamera.nonn,pkg.libcamera.noqt,nodoc`.

Branch layout
-------------

This branch carries the packaging recipe and the GitHub Actions
workflows that exercise it:

  * `debian/`            - the recipe.
  * `.github/workflows/` - `_build.yml` (reusable build),
                           `ci.yml` (transient validation),
                           `release.yml` (durable publish).
  * `.github/keys/`      - pinned RPi apt archive keyring used by
                           sbuild via `--extra-repository-key=`.

The workflow files live here, rather than on the repository's
default branch, because GitHub Actions resolves `pull_request` and
tag-push triggers from the base branch's workflow files. Hosting
them on `kurokesu` would prevent PRs targeting `debian/latest` from
triggering CI.

When `_build.yml` is later lifted to a shared `Kurokesu/ci-workflows`
repository, this directory shrinks to the two thin caller files only.

Identity adaptations
--------------------

These define Kurokesu's fork:

  * Version scheme: `0.7.1+rpt<date>+krks<N>-<M>`. The `+krks<N>`
    counter resets on each RPi resync. `-<M>` is the Debian packaging
    revision.
    Retire when: never (defines the fork).
  * `Maintainer`, `Uploaders`, `Vcs-*`, `watch`, `gbp.conf` repointed
    to github.com/Kurokesu/libcamera.
    Retire when: never (defines the fork).

Build-environment deviations (retirable)
----------------------------------------

pkg.libcamera.nonn profile
  Why:         bookworm lacks libtensorflow-lite-dev (NN-AWB).
  Retire when: bookworm dropped, or libtensorflow-lite-dev reaches the
               RPi bookworm archive.

noqt wired through d/rules
  Why:         RPi declared pkg.libcamera.noqt in debian/control
               (guarding qt6-base-dev) but debian/rules never read the
               profile, so requesting it dropped the build-dep yet
               still passed -Dqcam=enabled and failed dep-resolution.
  Retire when: RPi merges the same fix to pios/trixie.

python3-packaging <!nocheck>
  Why:         test/v4l2_compat/v4l2_compat_test.py imports
               `from packaging import version`. That module is not
               in bookworm's build chroot, so the test errored out
               instead of reaching its normal "no devices" skip.
  Retire when: RPi adds the build-dep upstream, or bookworm dropped.

Seed
----

  * Source: github.com/raspberrypi/libcamera, branch `pios/trixie`.
  * Last seed: 896780d3 (libcamera 0.7.1+rpt20260429-1).
  * Reseed procedure (in order):
      1. Replace `debian/` wholesale with the new seed's contents.
      2. Run `quilt push -a` against the merged source to verify our
         patches still apply (RPi refreshes patches between syncs and
         our merges may collide - refresh or replace any failures).
      3. Reapply this file's deviations.
      4. Update the "Last seed" SHA above in the same commit as the
         reseed.
      5. Bump `+krks<N>` and `-<M>` per project versioning rules
         (see project plan, not restated here).
      6. Prepend a new `debian/changelog` entry summarizing what the
         reseed brings in.
      7. Build on every supported suite (see "Supported suites").

Releasing
---------

Releases are paired tags:

  * `kurokesu` is tagged with `v<upstream-version>` - revision-less,
    e.g. `v0.7.1+rpt20260429+krks1`.
  * `debian/latest` is tagged with `debian/<full-version>` - carries
    the Debian revision, e.g. `debian/0.7.1+rpt20260429+krks1-1`.

Packaging-only rebuilds (`-2`, `-3`) reuse the source tag - only
the packaging tag moves.

To release, run `./release.sh` from this branch (use `--dry-run` to
preview). It derives both tag names from `debian/changelog` on the
remote packaging tip, reuses the source tag on packaging-only
rebuilds and pushes both tags atomically. The packaging-tag push
triggers `.github/workflows/release.yml`.

Manual equivalent (what the script automates):

  1. Tag the source on `kurokesu` with `v<upstream-version>`.
  2. Tag this branch with `debian/<full-version>`.
  3. Push both tags.

Release assets: per-suite tarballs (runtime debs plus that build's
`.changes`/`.buildinfo`) and `SHA256SUMS`. dbgsym debs and the
source package stay in workflow artifacts only, so `.changes`
entries for dbgsym files have no matching file in the tarball -
expected, not a defect.

Bookworm binaries carry a `~bpo12+1` version suffix appended at
build time (Debian backports convention, matching RPi's own archive
practice). This keeps deb filenames unique across suites in a shared
APT pool and makes a bookworm-to-trixie OS upgrade prefer the trixie
build. The changelog, tags and orig tarball stay suite-free.

Editing rule
------------

Any Kurokesu-specific change to the recipe (e.g. `debian/control`,
`debian/rules`, `debian/patches/`, `debian/*.install`, or other files
under `debian/`) must update the deviations section above in the
same commit.
